meta {
  name: 5 Request a new time (customer)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}
post {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/booking/appointments/{{appointmentIdentifier}}/reschedule-request
  body: json
}
body:json {
  {
    "newStartUtc": "2026-09-21T14:00:00Z"
  }
}
docs {
  A **customer** proposing a new time. **The appointment does not move.**

  The response still carries the original `start`; the proposal sits alongside it as `proposedStart` +
  `proposedBy`, and `appointmentStatus` becomes `5` (`RescheduleRequested`). Until the other party
  answers, every calendar keeps showing the session where it still is — a proposal is not an agreement.

  Pick the time from `GET /api/v1/calendar/availability/{email}` and send the server's own UTC instant
  back unchanged, so an approval is one tap and the slot was known free when it was picked. It is
  re-checked at approval: availability at proposal time is not a reservation.

  `409` when the session is not `Booked`, when a request is **already awaiting an answer** (refused
  rather than silently replacing the first, so neither party answers a proposal the other replaced),
  when the time is in the past, or when it is the time already booked.
}
